# CODEOWNERS for MicroZen
#
# This file maps paths in the repository to the owners responsible for
# reviewing changes to them. When a pull request touches a path, GitHub
# automatically requests a review from the matching owner(s).
#
# IMPORTANT: The handles below are PLACEHOLDERS. They will NOT take effect
# until a maintainer replaces them with real GitHub teams or users (and the
# teams exist in the MicroZenHub organization with write access to this repo).
# Replace handles such as @MicroZenHub/backend with your actual teams/users.
#
# Ordering note: later, more specific patterns override earlier ones, so rules
# are listed general-to-specific. The last matching pattern for a given file
# wins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owners for everything in the repo (most general rule).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                       @MicroZenHub/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and project knowledge: docs owners.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/README.md              @MicroZenHub/docs
/AGENTS.md              @MicroZenHub/docs
/docs/                  @MicroZenHub/docs
/.kiro/                 @MicroZenHub/docs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI, automation, and repo configuration: maintainers / devops.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/               @MicroZenHub/devops
/scripts/               @MicroZenHub/devops
/docker-compose.yml     @MicroZenHub/devops

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend (.NET solution): back-end owners (most specific rule).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/core/csharp/           @MicroZenHub/backend
